a racist display at a henderson shopping  mall shocking many in the community mary  jane bellies joining us live from the  galleria to explain the outrage mary  tayne  heather good afternoon to you community  leaders filled the galleria mall parking  lot this morning to protest a racist  display that was up for several weeks  stating racism is not welcomed in our  community the national action network  and other civil rights organizations are  outraged the network is reporting the  racist display was shown in front of  families and children from may 30 to  july 5th the display by las vegas  railway society shows a black man being  prepared to be hung robert bush the  local president of the national action  network says the goal of monday's  protest is to show the community that  racism will not be tolerated and they  are demanding an apology  not only was it racist but but there are  better ways  to depict black people in their history  of the railways such as blacks were the  first porters such as blacks built most  of the railways throughout the united  states if they wanted to show history in  the united states then there was a much  better way to be able to do that than  than a racist display  galleria mall general manager did offer  an apology bush tells me the las vegas  railway society has not yet responded  initially this was reported to the las  vegas action network through email that  display was taken down last week  reporting from sunset and stephanie  street mary jane balleza live local now  mary jane thank
 

